            <ArticleTitle>Atrial flutter a manifestation of cardiac tamponade.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e97-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1540-8159.2011.03052.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atrial flutter (AFL) is a common arrhythmia that is associated with postpericardiotomy and pericarditis. The relationship of AFL with tamponade has rarely been reported. A case of AFL with acute pericarditis and cardiac tamponade is thus presented here.</AbstractText>
